== Other colours ==

Forest is the proposal's default. Seven more colours, each dark and light, are on the [[https://samueloph.dev/debian-distributary-theme/|showcase]], where the page can switch to any of them and offers its wallpapers to download in 51 sizes: [[https://samueloph.dev/debian-distributary-theme/#colours-violet|Violet]], [[https://samueloph.dev/debian-distributary-theme/#colours-midnight|Midnight]], [[https://samueloph.dev/debian-distributary-theme/#colours-red|Debian red]], [[https://samueloph.dev/debian-distributary-theme/#colours-teal|Rose on teal]], [[https://samueloph.dev/debian-distributary-theme/#colours-glacier|Glacier]], [[https://samueloph.dev/debian-distributary-theme/#colours-lineage|Lineage]] and [[https://samueloph.dev/debian-distributary-theme/#colours-silt|Silt]]. All but Lineage also come without the accent on the fork.

||[[attachment:colours.png|{{attachment:colours.png|Every colour, dark and light|width=1000}}]]||

Other colours can be picked in the [[https://samueloph.dev/debian-distributary-theme/editor/|palette editor]], which redraws the wallpaper as you change them. Any of these colours, or your own, can also be generated locally from the source: `./build.py --scheme violet svg` makes Violet's wallpapers in under a minute, `./build.py --scheme violet` the whole theme in Violet (`violet-even` is the version without the accent), and `./build.py --palette my-colours.json` builds a palette saved from the editor.

